  "instructions": [
    "Clean the king oyster mushrooms. Using a fork, shred the mushroom stems lengthwise to create a pulled, stringy texture. Set aside.",
    "In a medium bowl, whisk together the soy sauce, maple syrup, liquid smoke, lime juice, smoked paprika, chili powder, cumin, garlic powder, and onion powder to create the marinade.",
    "Add the shredded mushrooms to the marinade and toss thoroughly to ensure they are all evenly coated. Let them marinate for at least 10-15 minutes to absorb the flavors.",
    "Heat the vegetable oil in a large skillet or pan over medium-high heat.",
    "Once the oil is hot, add the marinated mushrooms to the skillet in a single layer. Cook for 15-20 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the liquid has evaporated and the mushrooms are browned and slightly crispy on the edges.",
    "While the mushrooms are cooking, warm the corn tortillas. You can do this in a dry skillet for 30 seconds per side, over a gas flame for a slight char, or wrapped in a damp paper towel in the microwave.",
    "Assemble the tacos by filling each warm tortilla with a generous portion of the spicy pulled mushrooms.",
    "Garnish with your favorite toppings, such as sliced avocado, thinly sliced red onion, and fresh cilantro. Serve immediately with extra lime wedges on the side for squeezing."
  ],
  "notes": "For a creamy element, whip up a quick avocado crema by blending avocado, lime juice, cilantro, and a pinch of salt. These tacos are also excellent with a topping of crisp, fresh cabbage slaw.",
